  "limits": [
    "No live probe, HTTP request, GPU/NVML/Torch import, native/model/cache payload byte read, or fixture rerun occurred. Only this new audit file was written.",
    "Source pins and final integrity checks are joined from saved config, freeze, launch, actor and closure evidence. Current runtime source, native/interpreter binaries and weight bytes were not reread.",
    "The minimum over 70 accepted postlaunch samples is an online scalar from reviewed, pinned code. All 53 loop rows are retained; 15 readiness and 2 preexec rows lack standalone raw records. This audit cannot independently recompute all 70 values or establish a continuous-time minimum. Initial and final host rows are separate.",
    "Raw /proc limits lines are not retained. Manager settings and guarded readback values are verified from saved evidence; soft/hard limit text was not independently reparsed. CPU 0 denotes observed main-thread affinity, without a permanent all-thread or cpuset enforcement claim.",
    "The 64 MiB cap covers only the own-process PyTorch caching allocator. It excludes context, driver, cuBLAS and global physical UMA allocations. The 2 GiB unit limit and peak concern cgroup accounting; process peak RSS is a distinct metric. Neither limits every GPU or driver page.",
    "Global CUDA free memory is shared and sampled non-atomically. Pre-init free memory is unmeasured. CUDA free bytes must not be added to host MemAvailable, and these observations do not establish an owned or causal GPU-memory delta.",
    "After empty_cache, the saved allocator still reports 32 MiB allocated and the context remains initialized. This does not prove context destruction. Authenticated live-wrapper stop and saved unit/cohort exit establish process-lifetime closure, without proving restoration of all global driver/cache allocations.",
    "Five opaque CUDA cache files were enumerated but excluded from byte reads and hashes. Their contents remain local-only and outside this audit/Git payload allowlist. The JSON/text immutability claim covers 24 evidence files only.",
    "Controller exit 0 and actor entry exit 0 are distinct from a natural wrapper exit: the live wrapper was intentionally stopped before fallback exit 125. Closure covers the exact authenticated unit and observed cohort; it does not prove a universal process tree or prevent cgroup escape.",
    "This result covers only the fixed-GPU context, tiny 16\u00d716 BF16 operator and saved 512-byte closed-form hash evidence. It does not qualify model/header/payload/mmap loading, 12B, 8192 context, 20-second latency, N3/Q95, browser quality or benchmark scores."
  ],
